This disclosure concerns lightweight formulations suited for producing automotive parts, including molded components, along with various other manufactured items. These formulations include the following elements:

(a) A polyolefin material consisting of polypropylene, a propylene-ethylene block copolymer, or a mixture of both, where this polyolefin blend constitutes approximately 53% to 65% by weight of the total composition;

(b) A combination of two elastomers plus an impact-modifying compatibilizer, with these three components together making up roughly 27% to 32% by weight of the overall composition;

(c) A filler material accounting for about 5% to 12% by weight of the total composition; and

(d) A package of additives representing approximately 0.5% to 5% by weight of the formulation.
